39,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The financial data is quite sobering. We are paying for empty space, and every single change to the layout incurs a specific cost per desk. We must be very precise with our plan to avoid wasting budget.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that the area by the printer is much noisier in the afternoon. Also, the physio said it takes a long time to get our chairs and desks feeling just right for our bodies.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,May,,"It turns out the ""smooth"" morning upstairs takes up to nine minutes per person just to get settled! Plus, our arrival times are all over the place, so ""first-come, first-served"" is a total myth.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"So, the survey confirms that everyone wants a window, yet the plan only gives four people one. Meanwhile, our history of ""unplanned shuffles"" shows we're terrible at adapting without a total mess. We're heading for a conflict.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found that when people sit close, they talk more and share things naturally. The new joiners said they learned a lot just by overhearing us. Maybe we should prioritize that... the human connection.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, I agree that connection is valuable, but we must balance it with the fact that we are paying for space we aren't using. We cannot afford a trial-and-error approach given the per-desk relocation costs.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I understand the cost, but if we pick a spot that's too noisy or uncomfortable, won't that make us less productive? I'm worried that if we don't consider the feeling of the seat, we'll just want to move again.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, exactly! And let's not forget those nine minutes of setup time. If we choose a layout that requires constant tweaking or shifting, we're just eating into our actual work time every single morning. That's a hidden cost, right?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, you're finally thinking about costs, though in the most trivial way possible. The real cost here is the inevitable resentment when three of us are stuck staring at a wall while others enjoy the view. Who's taking the hit?","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I don't want anyone to feel resentful. But if we sit in a way that helps us support each other, maybe the view won't matter as much? I just... I want us to be close.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, resentment is a risk, but financial instability is a certainty if we are careless. We are paying for empty desks; perhaps we should consider if we actually need the current footprint or if we can optimize it.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, if we optimize the space, can we make sure the remaining spots are the most comfortable ones? I'm worried that if we just shrink the area, we might end up in the noisy parts.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,May,,"@Victoria, optimizing sounds great, but let's not make it a chore. If we're shrinking the footprint, let's make sure it doesn't add more setup hassle to our mornings. I can't imagine spending ten minutes just to start my day!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, optimizing the footprint doesn't solve the basic math of the window problem. We're still talking about a limited number of ""good"" seats. Let's stop dancing around it and decide how we're allocating the bad ones.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think we're focusing too much on the bad seats. If we arrange ourselves so we can actually talk and help each other, maybe the ""bad"" spots won't feel so lonely or frustrating?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, your optimism is noted, but we must be pragmatic. @Shunichi, the ""bad"" seats are a matter of preference, whereas the budget is a hard limit. Let's see the options and find a compromise that is fiscally responsible.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I hope the options let us think about the noise and the chairs too. If we can all be comfortable and not feel tired by the afternoon, I think we'll all be much happier.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm just hoping the options aren't too complicated! If we're going to move, let's make sure it's a one-and-done deal. I've had enough of ""temporary"" fixes that just waste our time. Let's see the plans!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"One-and-done is a fantasy, May. We'll just be pretending to be satisfied until the next ""unplanned shuffle"" hits. Let's just see the options and figure out who's getting the wall.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I hope we can find a plan that makes us feel like a team. I'll be waiting to see the options, and I hope we can be kind to each other when we choose.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
