64,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Given the costs of re-running power and the waste of paying for empty space, Option C is the most fiscally responsible. It eliminates permanent assignments and allows us to optimize our footprint without costly re-runs.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I'm worried about Option C. If we move every day, we can't keep our chairs and desks adjusted to our bodies, and we might end up in the noisy spots without knowing.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,May,,"@Victoria, Option C is a nightmare! Remember those nine minutes of setup time? Doing that every single morning is a total waste of our lives. I'm voting for Option A; let's just pick a spot and stay there.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, Option A is just a recipe for long-term bitterness. We'd be permanently assigning the ""wall seats"" to a few unlucky people. If we're going to be honest about the inequality, Option B is the only rational choice.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm worried about Option C too. If we move every day, we might not sit near the same people, and it'll be harder to talk. I think Option A or B is better... but maybe B is fairer?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, @Daisuke, Option B sounds fair in theory, but it is a financial disaster. Rotating blocks would require constant re-running of power and network cables, incurring those per-desk charges repeatedly. We cannot afford that.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I didn't think about the cables. But if we choose Option A, can we please make sure we consider the noise and the chair settings? I really want us to feel cozy.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,May,,"@Victoria, you're making a great point about the budget, but Option C is still a non-starter for me. I'm not spending my mornings fighting with cables and screens. Option A is the only one that's actually efficient!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, you're treating the budget as the only hard limit, but human resentment is a hard limit too. If we go with A, we're just deciding who to alienate. B isn't ""constant"" re-running; it's a scheduled shift.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I don't want anyone to be alienated. But if Option B is too expensive, maybe we can make Option A work? If we just... talk about where we sit and help each other?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, a scheduled shift is still a change in layout, and the quote was clear: every change costs us. We are already paying for empty space; we cannot justify further waste. Option A is the only stable, cost-effective choice.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, if we go with Option A, can we promise to be very careful about who sits where? I don't want anyone to be stuck in the noisy area or feel uncomfortable in their seat.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,May,,"@Minato, exactly! Let's just set it up once, get it right, and then we can actually focus on our work instead of playing musical chairs. Option A is the only way to save our sanity and our mornings!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, your obsession with the budget is almost impressive, but you're ignoring the social cost. If we go with A, we're just pretending the wall seats don't suck. I'm sticking with B; it's the only honest way to handle the inequality.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I really don't want us to fight. If Option B is too expensive, maybe we can use Option A but just be very thoughtful about who sits where? I'll vote for A if it means we stay together.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Victoria,,It is clear that Option A is the only viable path that balances our budget with the need for stability. Let's commit to it and be mindful of each other's needs. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Minato,,"I'll vote for Option A too. As long as we promise to think about the noise and the chair settings so everyone feels comfortable, I think it's the best way to be happy.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,May,,I'm voting for Option A! No more morning chaos or wasting precious minutes on setup. Let's just get settled and get on with our lives. Option A it is!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I'll vote for Option B. You're all choosing the path of least resistance, which just means we're ignoring the resentment building in the corner. I'd rather pay a fee than pretend the wall doesn't exist.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'll vote for Option A. I think if we're thoughtful about it, we can make it work. I just want us to be close and support each other.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
